        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "Really nice and caring professor. LITTRANS 205 is obviously very reading-heavy but it's spaced out pretty well. There's like four exams throughout the semester and every test has opportunity for PLENTY of extra credit points. As long as you do the readings, this class is a breeze. ",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Terrible, don't take LITTRANS 204 from her.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 1
            },
            {
                "comment": "Really kind and caring professor, clear and interesting lectures and easy to talk to. One criticism is that the class focused too much on history as a literature class imo, other than that she's great.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "She's a great prof. LIT Trans 205 is very reading-heavy. but not a lot of homework or exams! The quizzes are not too hard. This class is great for a lit credit and I am learning a lot",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Listening comprehension course. Grading not really based on learning that specific skill, but on how well you already know Russian. Lose points on 7-9 hr take-home exams for grammatical mistakes or phonetically correct transcriptions w/ wrong spelling, or on &quot;pictures optional&quot; presentations for not including pictures! Arbitrary and demotivating.",
                "difficulty_rating": 5,
                "quality_rating": 2
            },
            {
                "comment": "Professor Evans-Romaine came to class each day with a positive attitude, and made the class very enjoyable! I'm a STEM major and needed a CommB, and this class was a great choice, even though I had no prior experience with Russian Literature. EC is available on all quizzes/exams, and if you just show up and do the reading, you'll get an A!",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Good lectures, gets a bit in the weeds sometimes. Books were interesting if you like literature",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "She's a really enthusiastic and energetic teacher! I had her at 955 am and she still found a way to capture my attention! She doesn't grade very hard and the tests are standard, she offers A LOT of help and is always willing to give more. She always has a smile on her face and that makes it more enjoyable to sit there for 50 minutes. HIGH recommend",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Spend most of class time discussing readings and doing quizzes/tests, not enough time learning the language! Very harsh grader compared to previous courses. Avoid her if you can!",
